    "463": {
      "date": "2026-10-12",
      "edition": "Monday 12 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "League rules",
          "heading": "Hajime Shoji admits League One lacked communication before eligibility U-turn",
          "body": "In late August, Japan Rugby League One backtracked on player registration rules that would have classed some Japanese passport-holders born abroad as foreigners, limiting their domestic opportunities. After legal challenges and a fierce backlash from players, the league's exception now covers those who acquired Japanese citizenship by May 2025. Managing Executive Director Hajime Shoji admitted the league had lacked communication with affected players. The rules were due to take effect in the 2026-27 season, which begins in December."
        },
